{"id": "EUVD-2026-59282", "enisaUuid": "ac4d0cc4-e07f-3f26-bc4f-138d90639b09", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsctp: fix addr_wq_timer race in sctp_free_addr_wq()\n\nsctp_free_addr_wq() previously removed addr_wq_timer using timer_delete()\nwhile holding addr_wq_lock. However, timer_delete() does not guarantee that\na currently running timer handler has completed.\n\nThis allows a race with sctp_addr_wq_timeout_handler(), where the handler\nmay still run after addr_waitq has been freed, acquire addr_wq_lock, and\naccess freed memory, leading to a use-after-free.\n\nFix this by calling timer_shutdown_sync() before taking addr_wq_lock.  This\nguarantees that any in-flight timer handler has finished and prevents the\ntimer from being re-armed during teardown, making subsequent cleanup safe.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:56:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:46", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5098308ad72f83f3b1a48c247dddab1695114bae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d49eff15261dd62e4fa3a316c26cb1f537a60464", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a8323fb2ab6cd6978f359daeed6688e0cadf32ba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3e5cac47519d77ad36b9c03a1df1536aaa0c4a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/976c19de0f22a857ba0112f39635f8fd7a257568"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72383", "GHSA-8hr4-pprj-6g53"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2dbc5bcf-b2df-37e3-89cd-3f2b29cd9b96", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "370fdeb1-937c-3e31-9030-3ba5db391a0c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4db67e808640e3934d82ce61ee8e2e89fd877ba8 <a8323fb2ab6cd6978f359daeed6688e0cadf32ba"}, {"id": "3d0dbc2c-66a0-3ff6-b1c9-a0e3384af228", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "78fbe2b2-7fab-3ca9-8605-54583df50aa3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4db67e808640e3934d82ce61ee8e2e89fd877ba8 <5098308ad72f83f3b1a48c247dddab1695114bae"}, {"id": "86d7c0f5-c7e4-3e3f-ae78-bfefe750cdbc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "88a560e6-cefe-3656-94e7-5418383ba216", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "8d2ed649-16df-3378-9dec-4dec168ae19a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4db67e808640e3934d82ce61ee8e2e89fd877ba8 <c3e5cac47519d77ad36b9c03a1df1536aaa0c4a1"}, {"id": "8db4f443-415c-3233-97f7-c1428b2926f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.7"}, {"id": "8dba8e43-c1f1-35e7-8800-16981ade03de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4db67e808640e3934d82ce61ee8e2e89fd877ba8 <d49eff15261dd62e4fa3a316c26cb1f537a60464"}, {"id": "c62d4ab9-6e4c-35a9-b478-26db53ffcd0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "d0c04057-c9c2-372e-8595-ea8d15ad9a84", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4db67e808640e3934d82ce61ee8e2e89fd877ba8 <976c19de0f22a857ba0112f39635f8fd7a257568"}, {"id": "dc2cf054-0784-3beb-bb8d-f41ed496a24b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d884fd77-a6f9-3b70-8b1a-2b6bb1a7e6b9", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}